    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1469">

                <pb facs="1185" n="1069" xml:id="pg1069"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2171.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Commanding Officer Terhune of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Annapolis</hi>
                    telegraphed the Navy Department on December 9 as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>If Nicaraguan conditions remain as at present, I recommend withdrawal of
                            the marines about January 15, temporarily retaining 50 marines at
                            Managua, attached to the station-ship at Corinto, as a guard for the
                            Legation. Long concurs.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The foregoing is sent for your comment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
